            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0338" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.52/340: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-05T16:00:00+01:00">February 5, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 6—3:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>402. See my 389, February 4. Under Secretary Foreign Affairs assures me
                    instructions have been issued to Ministry Industry and Commerce and other
                    interested agencies to immediately suspend all exports of wolfram to any
                    destination pending preparation of counter proposals to our request for wolfram
                    embargo. Although he stated he is not in a position to divulge nature of these
                    counter proposals he has the impression they include an agreement on the part of
                    the Spanish Government to limit exports to Germany to a quantity not exceeding
                    exports during 1943.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
